# data directory
data/

# ...but DO track the committed golden test fixtures (small real BAM/FASTA + built h5)
!tests/data/
!tests/data/**

# ...and the library suite's fragment_array fixtures, for the same reason: they
# are gitignored by the blanket `data/` above, so a clean checkout errored 20
# tests in test/fragment_array/ with FileNotFoundError. 624 KB total, byte-identical
# to fragments_h5/tests/data (md5-verified), which is where they were recovered from.
!test/fragment_array/data/
!test/fragment_array/data/**

# ...and the specific fixtures in test/data/. Deliberately an explicit whitelist
# rather than `!test/data/**`, unlike the two blocks above: those directories
# hold nothing but fixtures, whereas test/data/ is ALSO where the suite writes
# its own residue — reader-cache artifacts named `<md5>_test.bb_chr1:200-302.bed.gz`
# plus random-named tempfiles. A `**` exception un-ignores that residue too, so
# it starts showing up in `git status` and one `git add -A` commits it.
# Note the idiom: un-ignore the directory so git will descend into it, then
# re-ignore its contents, then whitelist the fixtures by name. `!test/data/`
# alone is NOT enough — the blanket `data/` above matches only the directory,
# so negating it un-ignores everything inside.
!test/data/
test/data/*
!test/data/*.txt
!test/data/tss.synthetic.hg19.bed.gz


